    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Steam Vents on turn 1 when there are no 1-mana spells in hand wastes 2 life (if paid) or a turn of tempo (if not paid). Spirebluff Canal enters untapped for free with ≤2 other lands, making it the ideal turn 1 play. Spirebluff Canal's free-untapped window is limited to the first 3 land drops, while Steam Vents can always enter untapped later for 2 life, so sequencing Canal first preserves the most optionality.",
      "action_taken": "Played Steam Vents as the turn 1 land drop",
      "better_line": "Play Spirebluff Canal turn 1 (enters untapped for free), save Steam Vents for a later turn when the 2 life cost or tapped entry matters less",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 9,
      "player": "Haiku Truth",
      "decision_index": 8,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "The opponent has no creatures to block. Attacking with both Burnout Bashtronaut and Hired Claw would deal 3 total damage (1 from Bashtronaut combat, 1 from Hired Claw combat, and 1 from Hired Claw's Lizard attack trigger) instead of just 1 damage from Bashtronaut alone. There's no meaningful risk since the opponent has only 1 untapped land and no blockers.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked with only Burnout Bashtronaut for 1 damage.",
      "better_line": "Attack with both Burnout Bashtronaut and Hired Claw to deal 3 damage total into an empty board.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 20,
      "player": "Grok4F Libby",
      "decision_index": 15,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Island instead of Spirebluff Canal is suboptimal. With only 1 other land in play (Steam Vents), Spirebluff Canal would enter untapped and produce both U and R. Playing a basic Island now wastes the window where Spirebluff Canal enters untapped (it needs 2 or fewer other lands). Later when they have 3+ lands, Spirebluff Canal will enter tapped. Island provides only U, while Spirebluff Canal would provide U or R, giving better mana flexibility. The player also has Agna Qel'a which needs a basic land to enter untapped, so saving the Island for a later turn when they play Agna Qel'a would be better sequencing.",
      "action_taken": "Played basic Island as their land for turn 2.",
      "better_line": "Play Spirebluff Canal, which enters untapped with 1 other land and provides U/R flexibility. Save basic Island for a future turn to enable Agna Qel'a to enter untapped.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 24,
      "player": "Haiku Truth",
      "decision_index": 18,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Three Steps Ahead costs {U} base plus additional spree costs: +{1}{U} to counter, +{3} to clone, or +{2} to draw two and discard. The minimum total cost is {1}{U}{U} (to counter) or {2}{U} (to draw). With only 2 lands (Steam Vents and Island), the player cannot pay for any spree mode - they'd need at least 3 mana. Even if they could cast it, casting a reactive counterspell on their own main phase with no target to counter is wasteful. They should have cast Accumulate Wisdom for {1}{U} to draw a card, or played a land first. Combustion Technique could also have been used to kill the Hired Claw (dealing 2 damage to a 1/2). The player's reasoning shows they don't understand the card's cost structure.",
      "action_taken": "Attempted to cast Three Steps Ahead during their own main phase with only 2 mana available, which likely cannot pay for any spree mode.",
      "better_line": "Cast Combustion Technique targeting Hired Claw (dealing 2 damage to a 1/2 creature, killing it before it can accumulate counters and deal repeated damage), or cast Accumulate Wisdom for card selection. Playing a land first (Spirebluff Canal untapped) would have opened up more options with 3 mana.",
      "type": "blunder",
