      "player": "Haiku Truth",
      "decision_index": 22,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Casting Lightning Helix in the precombat main phase with the opponent tapped out wastes an opportunity to sequence better. The player should cast creatures before combat (specifically Emberheart Challenger which has haste) and attack first, then use Lightning Helix post-combat if needed, or hold it to respond to threats. More importantly, casting Lightning Helix now uses all mana (R+W), preventing the player from deploying Emberheart Challenger (1R) or Hired Claw (R) this turn. Since the opponent is tapped out with no blockers, deploying a hasty Emberheart Challenger and attacking with all creatures would deal more damage this turn. Lightning Helix to face deals 3 damage + 3 life; Emberheart Challenger attacking would deal 2 damage plus enable more damage from existing creatures. The key issue is that casting Helix uses both colored mana sources, leaving the player unable to cast any creature this turn, whereas casting Emberheart Challenger (1R) leaves W open but no additional plays. Actually, with Inspiring Vantage (R/W) and Sacred Foundry (R/W), casting Helix uses both lands. Casting Emberheart Challenger costs 1R, also using both lands. So either way only one spell can be cast. However, Emberheart Challenger has haste and can attack this turn for 2 damage, plus Hired Claw triggers (1 damage from Lizard attack), plus Burnout Bashtronaut attacks. Deploying the creature and attacking is likely better board development than 3 damage + 3 life from Helix, especially when the opponent is tapped out and can't interact.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Lightning Helix targeting opponent for 3 damage and 3 life gain, using all available mana",
      "better_line": "Cast Emberheart Challenger (haste creature), then attack with Emberheart Challenger, Burnout Bashtronaut, and Hired Claw to maximize board presence and damage while the opponent is tapped out. Save Lightning Helix for a future turn as removal or a finishing burn spell.",
