      "decision_index": 27,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Attacking with only Burnout Bashtronaut (1/1 menace) instead of both creatures leaves damage on the table. The opponent has no untapped creatures to block, so both attackers would connect safely. Attacking with both deals 1 (Bashtronaut) + 1 (Hired Claw combat) + 1 (Hired Claw's Lizard attack trigger) = 3 damage instead of just 1 (Bashtronaut) + 0 = 1 damage. The Hired Claw's trigger fires whenever you attack with one or more Lizards, dealing 1 damage to the opponent, and then connecting for another 1 combat damage. Additionally, dealing damage with both creatures would allow the Hired Claw's activated ability ({1}{R}: put a +1/+1 counter) to be used post-combat, and would increase speed for Burnout Bashtronaut faster. There's no reason to hold back the Hired Claw when the opponent has no blockers.",
