    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Casting Emberheart Challenger in precombat main phase when holding Slickshot Show-Off and Burst Lightning. The opponent has Steam Vents untapped (2 mana available) with Combustion Technique and Accumulate Wisdom in graveyard (suggesting they play blue-red spells). Deploying the Challenger before combat means it could eat removal before attacking. More importantly, Slickshot Show-Off has flying and haste - playing it precombat and then casting Burst Lightning during combat would trigger its +2/+0 twice (once from Burst Lightning), allowing 3 damage through the air plus the Burst Lightning's 2 damage for 5 total, putting opponent to 6. However, Emberheart Challenger also has haste and prowess, and casting Burst Lightning during combat would trigger both prowess and valiant if targeting the Challenger. The opponent has only 1 untapped land (Steam Vents) so limited interaction available. The choice between Emberheart and Slickshot is close - Emberheart as a 2/2 haste with prowess is reasonable, but playing creatures before combat when holding combat tricks and the opponent might have instant-speed interaction is slightly suboptimal sequencing. Plotting Slickshot Show-Off for a bigger future turn was also an option.",
