      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 59,
      "player": "Haiku Truth",
      "decision_index": 58,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "At 5 life against an aggressive deck with flying Slickshot Show-Off and Hired Claw, casting Monument to Endurance taps out most mana (spending 3 of 4 available), leaving only 1 mana open and unable to hold up Three Steps Ahead's counter mode (costs 3 mana) against potentially lethal burn or pump spells next turn. Monument is a long-term value engine but may not provide enough immediate defensive benefit at such low life.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Monument to Endurance for 3 mana, leaving 1 mana open with no ability to counter threats",
      "better_line": "Hold up Three Steps Ahead in counter mode (3 mana) to protect against burn spells or key threats, possibly casting Accumulate Wisdom (2 mana) first to dig for answers if sequencing allows, or cast Combustion Technique on a key threat like Slickshot Show-Off (deals 2+2=4 damage with 2 Lessons in graveyard) to remove the flying attacker",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 74,
      "player": "Haiku Truth",
      "decision_index": 68,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Cast Three Steps Ahead while Monument to Endurance is still on the stack. The discard from Three Steps Ahead resolves BEFORE Monument enters the battlefield, so the Monument discard trigger won't fire. Additionally, Accumulate Wisdom with 3 Lessons in graveyard draws all 3 cards for just {U} (with Gran-Gran discount), which is far superior to Three Steps Ahead's draw-2-discard-1 for {1}{U}.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Three Steps Ahead (draw 2, discard 1 mode) while Monument to Endurance was on the stack, wasting the discard trigger and using more mana for fewer net cards.",
      "better_line": "Let Monument to Endurance resolve first, then cast Accumulate Wisdom for {U} to draw 3 cards (all 3 kept due to 3 Lessons in graveyard). This nets +3 cards for 1 mana and leaves mana open, with the option to cast Three Steps Ahead later to trigger Monument's discard ability.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 75,
      "player": "Haiku Truth",
      "decision_index": 69,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "At 5 life, Monument to Endurance on the stack is extremely dangerous - its 'each opponent loses 3 life' trigger on discard means just two discard triggers could be lethal. Haiku Truth had Three Steps Ahead available to counter it for {U}{U} (reduced by Gran-Gran with 3 Lessons in graveyard), using their two untapped blue sources. Instead they cast Accumulate Wisdom, letting the Monument resolve.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Accumulate Wisdom to draw 3 cards (with 3 Lessons in graveyard), allowing Monument to Endurance to resolve",
      "better_line": "Cast Three Steps Ahead choosing the counter mode to counter Monument to Endurance. At 5 life, preventing the artifact that can deal 3 damage per discard trigger is far more important than card draw.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 77,
      "player": "Haiku Truth",
      "decision_index": 71,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Attacking with Gran-Gran (1/2) into an opponent at 21 life while at 5 life yourself is pointless and risky. Gran-Gran's tap trigger draws and discards a card, which synergizes with Monument to Endurance - but all of Haiku Truth's lands are already tapped, so tapping Gran-Gran via attacking means it can't block next turn. At 5 life against an aggressive deck with Hired Claw (which deals damage when Lizards attack), losing a potential blocker is dangerous. The 1 damage to a 21-life opponent is negligible. However, the draw/discard trigger from Gran-Gran tapping does trigger Monument to Endurance, which could provide value (draw a card, treasure, or 3 life loss to opponent). With all lands tapped though, any cards drawn can't be cast this turn. The Monument trigger is the main justification, but risking the blocker at 5 life is questionable to dangerous.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked with Gran-Gran 1/2 into opponent at 21 life while at 5 life",
      "better_line": "Not attacking and keeping Gran-Gran back as a blocker. At 5 life against an aggressive deck, preserving blockers is critical. Gran-Gran can be tapped via other means or used defensively.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 83,
      "player": "Haiku Truth",
      "decision_index": 76,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Discarded Abandon Attachments instead of a redundant land (Spirebluff Canal or Steam Vents) when already at 6 lands. Abandon Attachments synergizes powerfully with Monument to Endurance on the battlefield - casting it to discard a card would draw 2 cards AND trigger Monument for an additional mode. This is a valuable engine piece when behind at 5 life.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Abandon Attachments to Gran-Gran's trigger",
      "better_line": "Discard Spirebluff Canal or Steam Vents (redundant 7th/8th land) and keep Abandon Attachments as an engine piece with Monument to Endurance",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 84,
      "player": "Haiku Truth",
      "decision_index": 76,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Opponent is at 5 life with all lands tapped. Grok4F Libby has Shock (2 damage) and Burst Lightning (2 damage) in hand, totaling 4 damage for 2 mana. With Hired Claw on board (1/2) that can attack and deal 1 damage from its Lizard attack trigger, that's 1 (trigger) + 1 (combat) + 2 (Shock) + 2 (Burst Lightning) = 6 damage, which is lethal against 5 life. Even without combat, casting Shock + Burst Lightning = 4 damage, then attacking with Hired Claw = 1 trigger + 1 combat = 2 more = 6 total. By casting Slickshot Show-Off first (2 mana), they spend their mana on a creature instead of using burn spells for lethal. With only Inspiring Vantage and Sacred Foundry (2 lands available after casting Show-Off costs 1R), they may not have enough mana remaining to cast both burn spells. Actually, let me recount lands: Inspiring Vantage and Sacred Foundry = 2 mana total. Slickshot costs 1R = 2 mana, leaving 0 mana for burn. They should have cast Shock (R) targeting opponent for 2 damage, then Burst Lightning (R) targeting opponent for 2 damage = 4 damage. Combined with Hired Claw attack (1 trigger + 1 combat = 2), that's 6 damage total against 5 life = lethal. Instead they cast a creature and can't burn the opponent out this turn.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Slickshot Show-Off for 1R, using all available mana on a creature",
      "better_line": "Cast Shock targeting Haiku Truth (2 damage) and Burst Lightning targeting Haiku Truth (2 damage) for 4 burn damage, then attack with Hired Claw for 1 Lizard trigger damage + 1 combat damage = 6 total damage, lethal against 5 life",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 90,
      "player": "Grok4F Libby",
      "decision_index": 78,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "At 2 HP, Haiku Truth activated Agna Qel'a (costing 3 mana + tap) for a draw-discard before casting Accumulate Wisdom. With 6 Lesson cards in graveyard and Gran-Gran's cost reduction, Accumulate Wisdom costs only {U} and draws ALL THREE top cards. Casting Accumulate Wisdom first would provide far more information and cards to work with before committing 3 mana to a draw-discard effect.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Agna Qel'a for {2}{U} to draw and discard, using 3 mana before seeing more cards.",
      "better_line": "Cast Accumulate Wisdom first for {U} (draws 3 cards with Lesson threshold met), then use remaining mana informed by the 3 new cards - potentially finding burn, counters, or better plays before committing to the Agna Qel'a activation.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 98,
      "player": "Haiku Truth",
      "decision_index": 84,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Casting Three Steps Ahead in response to their own Accumulate Wisdom on the stack, rather than letting Accumulate Wisdom resolve first. With 6 Lesson cards in graveyard, Accumulate Wisdom draws all 3 top cards - resolving it first gives more information about what's available before committing Three Steps Ahead's resources. At 2 life, resource efficiency is critical.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Three Steps Ahead in response to own Accumulate Wisdom before seeing the 3 cards from it",
      "better_line": "Let Accumulate Wisdom resolve first to draw 3 cards, then decide whether/how to use Three Steps Ahead with full information about available resources",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 99,
      "player": "Haiku Truth",
      "decision_index": 85,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Spirebluff Canal enters tapped because Haiku Truth controls more than 2 other lands, so it provides no mana this turn. At 2 life facing an aggressive opponent, maximizing available mana is critical for holding up interaction like Three Steps Ahead (counter mode) or multiple spells.",
      "action_taken": "Played Spirebluff Canal, which enters tapped and provides no mana this turn.",
      "better_line": "Play Island instead, which enters untapped, providing an additional mana this turn for more flexible interaction. This allows casting multiple spells or holding up more defensive options at a critical 2 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 104,
      "player": "Haiku Truth",
      "decision_index": 91,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "At 2 life against an aggressive deck with creatures that just attacked, Haiku Truth is in a desperate position. They have 7 cards in graveyard that are Lessons (3x Combustion Technique, 3x Accumulate Wisdom, 1x Abandon Attachments = 7 Lesson cards, with 3+ being Lessons), meaning Gran-Gran's cost reduction is active. Artist's Talent is a slow enchantment that doesn't impact the board or help survive. The opponent has Hired Claw and Slickshot Show-Off that will untap next turn. At 2 life, Haiku Truth needs to either develop instant-speed interaction or find removal. Abandon Attachments (discard + draw 2) with Monument to Endurance on board would generate significant card advantage and potentially find answers, while also triggering Monument's abilities. Three Steps Ahead could be held up to counter a lethal burn spell. Casting Artist's Talent uses mana on a do-nothing enchantment when at 2 life facing lethal next turn.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Artist's Talent, a slow Class enchantment that provides no immediate board impact or survival benefit.",
      "better_line": "Cast Abandon Attachments (costs only U/R with Gran-Gran's cost reduction active since 3+ Lessons in graveyard), discarding a card to draw 2 and triggering Monument to Endurance, then hold up remaining mana for Three Steps Ahead or Spell Snare to counter any burn spell that would be lethal.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 105,
      "player": "Haiku Truth",
      "decision_index": 92,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Haiku Truth had Spell Snare in hand which perfectly counters Artist's Talent (mana value 2) on the stack, AND had enough mana to cast both Spell Snare and Abandon Attachments (with Gran-Gran's cost reduction making Abandon Attachments cost just {U/R}). Two untapped lands (Steam Vents + Spirebluff Canal) could pay for both. Instead, they let Artist's Talent resolve, giving the opponent a powerful value engine with card filtering and potential damage amplification.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Abandon Attachments in response to Artist's Talent, letting the enchantment resolve.",
      "better_line": "Cast Spell Snare targeting Artist's Talent to counter it (spending {U}), then cast Abandon Attachments with the remaining untapped land (costs {U/R} with Gran-Gran's reduction). This accomplishes both objectives: denying the opponent their value engine AND getting the Monument to Endurance trigger.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 106,
      "player": "Haiku Truth",
      "decision_index": 93,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "At 2 life against an aggressive Boros deck, declined to counter Artist's Talent (mana value 2) with Spell Snare. Artist's Talent provides card filtering immediately, cost reduction at level 2, and critically at level 3 adds +2 to all noncombat damage — making even a Shock lethal. The game offered Spell Snare as a valid castable option, meaning mana was available.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without casting any spells, allowing Artist's Talent to resolve.",
      "better_line": "Cast Spell Snare targeting Artist's Talent to prevent the opponent from gaining incremental advantage and potentially game-ending damage amplification at level 3.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 109,
      "player": "Haiku Truth",
      "decision_index": 98,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "At 2 life, letting Artist's Talent resolve is very dangerous. Its Level 3 ability adds +2 to all noncombat damage, meaning any Shock or Burst Lightning becomes lethal. Spell Snare perfectly counters this mana value 2 enchantment. Even if Haiku Truth couldn't cast Spell Snare due to mana constraints, the reasoning shows they simply wanted to 'pass priority to move to combat' without even considering the threat on the stack.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, allowing Artist's Talent to resolve without attempting to counter it.",
      "better_line": "Cast Spell Snare targeting Artist's Talent to counter it, preventing the opponent from gaining card filtering, cost reduction, and the potentially lethal +2 noncombat damage bonus at Level 3.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 110,
      "player": "Haiku Truth",
      "decision_index": 99,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "At 2 life facing lethal on board next turn, Haiku Truth passed priority without casting any spells. With 7+ Lesson cards in graveyard and Gran-Gran's cost reduction active, Abandon Attachments and potentially other spells were castable. Abandon Attachments would discard a card (triggering Monument to Endurance for draw/treasure/3 life loss to opponent) and draw 2 cards, helping dig for removal or interaction to survive. Passing here likely means dying next turn without attempting to find answers.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting any spells at 2 life",
      "better_line": "Cast Abandon Attachments, discarding a card to draw 2 and trigger Monument to Endurance (choosing draw or treasure for mana), then potentially chain more spells to find removal like Burst Lightning or Shock to deal with opponent's creatures before they attack for lethal",
      "type": "blunder",
